   "At Christmas 1914, British and German soldiers spontaneously stopped fighting in places to exchange gifts and sing: the \"Christmas truce\".",
   "The steel helmet, thought of as typical of the war, only appeared in 1915; before that, French soldiers wore a kepi and very visible red trousers.",
