   "Germany's Enigma codes were broken by a British team including mathematician Alan Turing, building on the work of Polish cryptologists.",
   "Navajo soldiers used their language as a secret code for US communications: the Japanese never cracked it.",
   "Penicillin, mass-produced during the war, saved thousands of wounded soldiers.",
   "8 May is a public holiday in France, and 27 January is International Holocaust Remembrance Day.",
   "The diary of Anne Frank, a Jewish girl who hid in Amsterdam and died after deportation, is one of the most-read books in the world."
